-- title:
--   Corner modules at Γ_H(Mr) and Γ₀(Mr) coincide
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p\neq 2$ a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and $\bar\rho$ a residual representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a rank-two space over the residue field, factoring through a finite level, absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field has no proper invariant subspace. Hypotheses on the level are summarised as follows: $S$ is a finite set of primes containing $p$; $M\neq 0$ has all prime divisors in $S$ and $p^2\nmid M$; $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ contains $p$ and, for $q\neq p$, $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$; every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $M$, every $q\neq p$ dividing $M$ outside $S_{\min}$ divides $M$ at least twice, no $q\neq p$ divides $M$ three times; inertia at each $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ if $p\mid M$. Further, $\theta$ is a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ (for a level admitting an integral structure) to the residue field with $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M$; and $r$ is a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid M$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ at every Frobenius at $r$. Set $L=M r$ and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$. Two sets of corner data are given for the cohomology modules $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ and $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(L),\mathcal O)$ (the case $H=\top$): commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras $\mathbb T$, $\mathbb T'$, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, acting compatibly; idempotent splittings $Sp$, $Sp'$ with indices $i$, $i'$, whose corner submodules $e_i\cdot H^1$ are finite free over $\mathcal O$; maps $\mathrm{tfull}$, $\mathrm{tfull}'$ from the generator type $\mathrm{Gen}\,L\,S$ (operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$, operators $U_q$ for primes $q\mid L$, and diamonds $\langle d\rangle$) to $\mathbb T$, $\mathbb T'$, and a single map $\mathrm{cfull}$ to $\mathcal O$. For all guarded generators $g$, that is all $g$ that are not $U_q$ for a prime $q\mid L$ with $q\nmid M$: every element of $\mathbb T$ (resp. $\mathbb T'$) acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ of the guarded generators; $\mathrm{tfull}\,g$ acts as $\mathrm{opFamily}\,g$; $\mathrm{tfull}\,g-\mathrm{cfull}\,g$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_i$ of the splitting; and the corner submodules are cofull, containing every $v$ for which suitable powers of $\mathrm{tfull}\,g-\mathrm{cfull}\,g$ carry $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1$ for all $k$. The scalars satisfy: the residue of $\mathrm{cfull}(T_\ell)$ is $\theta(T_\ell)$; $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal when $q\mid M$, $q\neq p$, $q^2\mid M$; $\mathrm{cfull}(U_p)$ is a unit when $p\mid M$; and $\mathrm{cfull}(\langle d\rangle)\equiv 1$. Both corner submodules are non-zero and both corner rings $e_i\mathbb T e_i$, $e_{i'}\mathbb T' e_{i'}$ act faithfully on them. Finally $h_1$ is the degeneracy datum $\mathrm{LevelLE}\,L\,L\,\top\,H\,1$, so that $\mathrm{iDegL}$ is restriction of homomorphisms along $\Gamma_H(L)\subseteq\Gamma_0(L)$. The conclusion asserts four things: the corner submodule at level $\Gamma_H(L)$ is exactly the image under this restriction map of the corner submodule at level $\Gamma_0(L)$; the restriction map is injective on the latter corner; the two corner submodules have equal $\mathcal O$-ranks; and there is an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e_D$ from $e_i\mathbb T e_i$ to $e_{i'}\mathbb T' e_{i'}$ sending the corner image of $\mathrm{tfull}\,g$ to that of $\mathrm{tfull}'\,g$ for every guarded $g$, and compatible with the restriction map in the sense that restriction of $e_D(x)\cdot a$ equals $x$ applied to the restriction of $a$.
--
--   This is the descent along the diamond group $\Delta=\Gamma_0(L)/\Gamma_H(L)\cong(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$ at the auxiliary level $L=Mr$: when $p\nmid r-1$, the index $[\Gamma_0(L):\Gamma_H(L)]=r-1$ is invertible in $\mathcal O$ and the residually trivial diamond operators act trivially on the corner, so restriction identifies the two localised cohomology modules together with their Hecke actions. It feeds the comparison of free ordinary corners at level $Mr$, the rank computations for the auxiliary-level corner modules, and the construction of the corner-ring isomorphism used in the Taylor–Wiles patching argument.
